# Week 2 Learning Journey: AWS Compute & Networking ☁️

During Week 2 of my cloud internship, I explored the core building blocks of AWS infrastructure. The focus was on understanding how cloud servers, networking, and security work together to host applications reliably and securely.

---

## 🖥️ Amazon EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)

Amazon EC2 allows users to launch virtual servers in the cloud within minutes. Instead of purchasing physical hardware, organizations can rent computing resources on demand.

### What I Learned

* What EC2 instances are and why they are used
* Different instance types and their use cases
* Amazon Machine Images (AMIs)
* Key Pairs for secure access
* Elastic Block Store (EBS) for persistent storage

### Hands-On Practice

* Launched a Linux EC2 instance
* Connected to the instance using SSH
* Explored the AWS Management Console
* Monitored instance status and performance

---

## 🌐 Amazon VPC (Virtual Private Cloud)

A VPC is a private network created within AWS where resources can be deployed securely.

### What I Learned

* Purpose of a VPC
* CIDR blocks and IP addressing
* Public and Private Subnets
* Route Tables
* Internet Gateway

### Architecture Overview

```text
Internet
   │
Internet Gateway
   │
 ┌─────────────┐
 │ Public      │
 │ Subnet      │
 │ Web Server  │
 └─────────────┘
   │
 ┌─────────────┐
 │ Private     │
 │ Subnet      │
 │ Database    │
 └─────────────┘
```

### Hands-On Practice

* Created a custom VPC
* Configured subnets
* Attached an Internet Gateway
* Updated Route Tables

---

## 🔒 Security Groups

Security Groups act as virtual firewalls that control inbound and outbound traffic for AWS resources.

### Common Rules

| Port | Service | Purpose                |
| ---- | ------- | ---------------------- |
| 22   | SSH     | Remote Access          |
| 80   | HTTP    | Website Traffic        |
| 443  | HTTPS   | Secure Website Traffic |

### What I Learned

* Difference between inbound and outbound rules
* Principle of least privilege
* Importance of securing cloud resources

### Hands-On Practice

* Created Security Groups
* Allowed SSH access from my IP address
* Configured HTTP traffic for web access

---

## ⚖️ Elastic Load Balancer (ELB)

Load Balancers distribute incoming traffic across multiple servers to improve availability and reliability.

### Benefits

* High availability
* Better fault tolerance
* Improved performance
* Traffic distribution across instances

### What I Learned

* Why load balancing is important
* How AWS routes requests to healthy instances
* Basic architecture of highly available applications

---

## 🎯 Auto Scaling

Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances based on demand.

### Benefits

* Cost optimization
* Better performance during peak traffic
* Improved reliability

### Example

```text
Low Traffic      → 1 Instance
Medium Traffic   → 2 Instances
High Traffic     → 4 Instances
```

### What I Learned

* Scaling policies
* Dynamic resource allocation
* Importance of elasticity in cloud computing

